  "term": "theory of mind",
  "definition": "Theory of mind is the ability to recognize that you and other people have mental states such as beliefs, desires, feelings, intentions, and thoughts, and to use that understanding to make sense of behavior. Differences or deficits in this ability are associated with conditions such as Asperger syndrome, autistic disorder, and schizophrenia.",
